"Let $\\mathcal{H}=(V,\\mathcal{E})$ be an $r$-uniform hypergraph on $n$ vertices. For a positive integer $k<r$, let $\\nu_k(\\mathcal{H})$ denote its $k$-matching number, and let $a\\geq2$ with $n\\geq r\\cdot a$. Set\n\n$$\nn_0=ra-(a-1)(k-1)-1.\n$$\n\nFor each integer $i$ satisfying\n\n$$\n0\\leq i\\leq\\frac{\\left\\lfloor\\frac{n}{a-1}\\right\\rfloor-k}{2},\n$$\n\nlet $\\mathcal{F}_i$ be a $(n,r,k,a,i)$-Frankl family. **Generalized Erdős' matching conjecture.** If $\\nu_k(\\mathcal{H})<a$, then\n\n$$\n|\\mathcal{E}|\\leq\\max\\left\\{\\binom{n_0}{r},|\\mathcal{F}_i|;\\ 0\\leq i\\leq\\frac{\\left\\lfloor\\frac{n}{a-1}\\right\\rfloor-k}{2}\\right\\}.\n$$\n\nThe claim extends the classical matching problem to $k$-matchings and proposes that the extremal examples are the complete $r$-uniform hypergraph on $n_0$ vertices and the indicated Frankl families. The supplied text gives no resolution status beyond its formulation, so the conjecture is recorded as open."